    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-seventh-year",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.1–7; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "At the beginning of his seventh year, Vināyaka bathes and performs daily rites. Crowned, lion-mounted, he bears goad, axe, lotus and fear-removing noose; staff/skin, gold jewelled earrings, waterpot, darbha, yellow silk, musk mark, crescent, pearl necklace and serpent at navel adorn him. Playful roar shakes heaven/earth; cātaka birds mistake thunder, rivers leap; Aditi and Kaśyapa rejoice and praise their ancestry’s fortune.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-wedding-commission",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.7–18; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Unnamed Kāśī king visits Kaśyapa, exchanges embraces/bows, receives seat and six-taste meal. Kaśyapa asks why king has neglected his purohita. King apologizes for royal preoccupation and personally requests performance of his son’s wedding. Kaśyapa declines because observing Cāturmāsya, offers capable son. King accepts; father sends Vināyaka despite separation sorrow; child bows parents and boards king’s chariot.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-aditi-entrustment",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.19–22; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Aditi tells king her child must be guarded constantly, since upheavals occur wherever he is; guard like eyelids the pupil, and return as received. King agrees, bows and departs with child by swift chariot into great forest.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-dhumraksa-tapas",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.23–27; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Forest belongs to Dhūmrākṣa, strong brother of Raudraketu and paternal uncle of Narāntaka. For10000years he worships thousand-rayed Sun, hanging feet from tree with head down and drinking smoke; requests supreme all-destroying weapon and subjection of three worlds. After long time Sun sends an unfailing radiant weapon toward the ascetic.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-sun-weapon-seized",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.27–32; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Vināyaka sees sky-filling brilliance, flies and catches weapon. King marvels and reflects that gain/loss/life depend on destiny. To ascertain its power child weighs/tosses weapon upwards; it falls roaring on Dhūmrākṣa, splitting him in two. Falling pieces crush rocks/trees and cover500bow-lengths of ground.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-sons-threat-king",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.33–43; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Dhūmrākṣa’s sons Jaghana and Manu attend their father, see his destruction, rush angrily and accuse king of bringing child to kill him. They say father formerly protected king from Narāntaka. King fears loss of kingdom, swears by brāhmaṇa/Īśvara that purohita’s son was brought only for wedding, asks no obstruction and offers child to them. Vināyaka protests handing a bound child to enemies, asks what king will tell parents and warns angry Kaśyapa could burn king.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-sons-breath-return",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.44–51; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Sons approach to devour him; child roars, shakes three worlds and breath propels them to cloud layer. After two muhūrtas Jaghana and Manu fall in Narāntaka’s city crushing houses. Amid commotion messengers inspect apparently dead sons, find both conscious, revive/attend them and hear their account: father killed by Kaśyapa’s son, selves thrown by breath, child travelling with Kāśī king. Messengers report to Narāntaka.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
      "verification_notes": "Author witness-level Sanskrit reading checked; independent Sanskrit expert/printed-edition verification pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "gkr2-e-thousand-host",
      "source_id": "gp-src-ganesha",
      "witness_id": "gp-wit-sd-krida",
      "passage_id": "gkr2-p-012",
      "locator": "Krīḍā 12.52–59; https://sanskritdocuments.org/doc_purana/gaNeshapurANam2.html",
      "paraphrase": "Narāntaka angrily sends1000rākṣasas to seize sage’s son, ordering death if he fights. The command also mentions Kāśī king’s chariot. They hasten, meet both travellers. Vināyaka’s fearsome roar kills some; others flee, suffer broken feet/heads/faces/eyes/thighs/arms, and arrow-torn bellies. Survivors reach Narāntaka and report.",
      "classification": "DIRECT_TEXT",
      "verification_status": "VERIFIED",
      "verifier": "Krīḍā continuation2 author, direct digital body reading",
